{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"TIA \u2014 device tree"},"description":"Hardware tree of a device (racks/slots/modules). Requires a connected project. For a large device read it in pages: pass limit (1-1000), then pass the nextCursor of each page as cursor until nextCursor is null. A page is {device, typeIdentifier, items, total, nextCursor}; total is the number of tree nodes of the whole device. A page is a forest: an item whose parent is on another page is listed at the top level of items with parentPath (the names of its ancestors, outermost first). Without limit and cursor the whole tree is returned. Each item's addresses [{start, length, ioType}] are the raw Openness values: start is a byte number and length is in BITS (an S7-1200 DI 14/DQ 10 input range of 2 bytes reads 16), not the byte length that tia_io_map answers. Maps to GET /devices/{device}/tree?limit=&cursor= (both optional). Read-only (class R).","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","properties":{"cursor":{"description":"the nextCursor of the previous page, passed back exactly as received; it is opaque, so never invent, build or edit one (omit it for the first page, and omit both limit and cursor for the whole list)","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"device":{"description":"device name","type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"page size, an integer from 1 to 1000; pass it to read the list in pages (omit both limit and cursor for the whole list)","maximum":1000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"}},"required":["device"],"type":"object"},"name":"tia_device_tree","outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":{},"definitions":{"__schema0":{"additionalProperties":{},"properties":{"addresses":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":{},"properties":{"ioType":{"type":"string"},"length":{"maximum":900719925474099